{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.skew_poisson_integration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skew_poisson_integration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skew_poisson_integration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skew_poisson_integration","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L49-L76","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\nLet $H/\\mathbb{F}_\\pp$ be a smooth commutative formal group and\n$\\pi_<$ a skewed-Poisson structure on $H$.  Then there exists a\n(generally non-commutative) formal group $G/\\mathbb{Z}_\\pp$ such that:\n\n1. $G \\otimes_{\\mathbb{Z}_\\pp} \\mathbb{F}_\\pp  \\cong  H$\n   (reduction modulo $\\pp$ recovers $H$);\n\n2. $\\mathrm{Dist}(G)$ is a deformation of\n   $\\mathrm{Dist}(H)$ computed via a\n   Grobner--Shirshov basis for the relations of the enveloping\n   algebra;\n\n3. the comultiplication on $\\mathrm{Dist}(G)$ satisfies the\n   *strong multiplicativity* condition: the Frobenius relation\n   $(\\mathrm{Id}\\otimes m)\\circ(\\Delta\\otimes\\mathrm{Id}) = \\Delta\\circ m$ is preserved under the deformation.\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skew-poisson-integration","label":"prop:skew-poisson-integration","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_iii_frobenius_preserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_iii_frobenius_preserved","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (iii): Frobenius relation is preserved\nunder the deformation `Frob_LHS = Frob_RHS`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.Frob_RHS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.Frob_RHS","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Frobenius RHS `Δ ∘ m` applied to `x : DistG`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.Frob_LHS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.Frob_LHS","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Frobenius LHS `(id ⊗ m) ∘ (Δ ⊗ id)` applied to `x : DistG`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_ii_distribution_deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_ii_distribution_deformation","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii): the deformation map is injective\n(Gröbner–Shirshov deformation preserves distinctness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.deformation","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Deformation map `Dist(H) → Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.DistH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.DistH","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Distribution algebra type `Dist(H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.DistG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.DistG","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Distribution algebra type `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_i_reduction_isomorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.claim_i_reduction_isomorphism","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i): `G ⊗_{ℤ_p} 𝔽_p ≅ H`. Captured as the\nexistence of bijections going each way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.G_mod_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.G_mod_p","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L26-L26","doc":"Reduction mod `p` of `G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.G","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L24-L24","doc":"The integrating non-commutative formal group `G/ℤ_p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.H","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Categorical object / monoidal structure (formal group `H`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegrationContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skew_poisson_integration.lean#L17-L47","doc":"Abstract context for the `skew_poisson_integration` claim — manuscript-themed\ntyped fields below; `claim_i` / `claim_ii` / `claim_iii` carry the three\nnumbered sub-claims of the manuscript proposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}